# Copy to deploy/failover.env (chmod 600) on the SECOND VPS only, and adjust the
# values for your domain. Read by deploy/failover-agent.sh and, through it,
# deploy/dns-failover.sh.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# deploy/failover-agent.sh promotes this node's standby and can move the public
# A record. Both of those are consequential enough that they must be reviewable
# and reversible WITHOUT editing a script, so every tunable lives here. Anything
# left unset falls back to the default in the right-hand column below.
#
# The agent sources this file with `set -a` semantics, so an already-exported
# variable wins. It deliberately does NOT live in .env.production: that file is
# the compose `env_file`, so touching it changes the compose config hash and
# would make stack-watchdog.sh recreate both API colours at once.
#
# This file is gitignored - it is host configuration, and it holds API tokens.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- identity ---
# Public hostname users reach the ERP on. Also the A record dns-failover.sh
# moves. Default: DOMAIN from .env.production.
#DOMAIN=hopedesign.jorlentech.com

# The DNS zone that hosts the record above. Default: jorlentech.com
#ZONE=jorlentech.com

# The public address of the PRIMARY. The agent treats this as the second,
# independent "is the primary really gone" probe: a promotion requires BOTH the
# WireGuard tunnel and this address to stop answering, so a tunnel-only flap can
# never mint a second writer.
#PRIMARY_PUBLIC_IP=23.239.220.214

# The public address of THIS node - the failover target. Required, with no
# default, because it is the address DNS is moved TO. dns-failover.sh refuses to
# point the record at an address that does not answer with the ERP health
# payload, so a wrong value here fails loudly rather than blackholing the site.
#PEER_PUBLIC_IP=

# ------------------------------------------------------ promotion threshold ---
# Where the primary's postgres listens on the tunnel.
#PRIMARY_WG_IP=10.77.0.1
#PRIMARY_PG_PORT=9101

# Consecutive failed checks before a promotion. The agent runs from cron every
# 2 minutes, so the default means roughly 6 minutes of confirmed, dual-path
# silence before this node takes over. Raise it if a brief network partition
# would be more expensive than a longer outage. Default: 3
#DOWN_CHECKS_REQUIRED=3

# THE SAFETY CATCH. Replication lag, in seconds, past which the agent refuses to
# promote and alerts a human instead. Promoting a standby that is minutes behind
# silently discards the difference - invoices and EFRIS submissions the primary
# accepted and answered OK. Refusing is always the safe failure: users see an
# outage, but the two copies stay reconcileable. Default: 300
#MAX_REPLAY_LAG_SECONDS=300

# ------------------------------------------------------------- automation ---
# Set to 0 to stop the agent promoting on its own. It will still detect and
# alarm, and `failover-agent.sh promote` remains available as a deliberate
# operator action. Worth setting to 0 before any planned work on the primary.
# Default: 1
#AUTO_PROMOTE=1

# Set to 0 to stop the agent moving the A record after a successful promotion.
# The promotion still happens; only the DNS step is left to a human. Default: 1
#AUTO_MOVE_DNS=1

# Start the background worker on this node once it has been promoted. Scheduled
# work must run exactly once cluster-wide, so the worker is profile-gated and
# normally exists only on the data primary - but after a promotion this node IS
# the data primary, and without the worker invoices, report schedules, the
# Hikvision drain and notification delivery all stop. Default: 1
#START_WORKER_ON_FAILOVER=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------- DNS mover ---
# Which provider dns-failover.sh talks to.
#
#   cloudflare  PATCHes the existing A record in place - one API call, touches
#               nothing else, and honours RECORD_TTL. This is the only provider
#               that can move the record in seconds. Needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#               (Zone.DNS:Edit) and either CF_ZONE_ID or a token that can read
#               /zones?name=ZONE.
#
#   namecheap   Uses setHosts, which REPLACES THE ENTIRE RECORD SET for the
#               zone. It refuses to run unless DNS_RECORDS below lists every
#               record you want kept - including MX, TXT and any other A/CNAME -
#               because a partial list would silently delete mail routing. The
#               write is immediate but resolvers cache the old address for up to
#               the old TTL, so expect a window measured in tens of minutes.
#
#   unset       The agent refuses to guess and raises a CRITICAL alert naming the
#               manual step. This is the safe default: it is far better to be
#               told "move the A record to X by hand" than to have a script
#               guess at a zone it does not fully understand.
#DNS_PROVIDER=cloudflare

# TTL applied to the A record, in seconds. Lower it BEFORE you need a failover:
# the cache lifetime during an outage is whatever is already published, so a
# 1799-second record means a ~30 minute window no matter what this is set to
# when the move happens. `dns-failover.sh lower-ttl` does that as a one-off.
# Default: 60
#RECORD_TTL=60

# Refuse to move the record to an address that does not answer with the ERP
# health payload. Leave this on: pointing DNS at a host that is not actually
# serving turns a recoverable outage into a total one. Default: 1
#REQUIRE_TARGET_HEALTHY=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------ credentials ---
# Cloudflare. Leave CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN unset if you use namecheap.
# Scope the token to Zone:DNS:Edit on ZONE only - not account-wide.
#CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Optional. Skips the extra /zones lookup. Find it on the zone's overview page.
#CF_ZONE_ID=

# Namecheap API. Requires API access enabled on the account and the calling IP
# whitelisted. NAMECHEAP_USER_NAME is the account username and
# NAMECHEAP_API_USER is normally the same value.
#NAMECHEAP_USER_NAME=
#NAMECHEAP_API_USER=
#NAMECHEAP_API_KEY=

# Required by the namecheap provider ONLY. The COMPLETE record set for ZONE, one
# per line, in Namecheap's own "name:type:address:ttl" form - setHosts replaces
# the whole set, so anything missing here is deleted. The A record for DOMAIN is
# rewritten by the agent; the rest are re-sent verbatim.
#
#DNS_RECORDS="
#@:A:23.239.220.214:60
#www:CNAME:jorlentech.com.:60
#@:MX:mx1.privateemail.com.:60
#@:TXT:v=spf1 include:spf.privateemail.com ~all:60
#"